{"question_id": "FQA-1373715-04", "event": "model_response", "turn": 6, "elapsed_seconds": 4.4019407001324, "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": "**ServiceNow, Inc. (CIK 1373715) — operating expense profile, FY2022–FY2024**\n\nAll figures are consolidated, full-year (10-K, fiscal years ended Dec 31), in USD. Source: FY2024 10-K filed 2025-01-30, accession 0001373715-25-000010 (comparative FY2022–FY2023 figures from the same filing agree with the prior 10-Ks).\n\n**Total operating expenses grew more slowly than revenue, so the expense ratio fell.**\n- Operating expenses: $5,317M (FY2022) → $6,288M (FY2023) → $7,333M (FY2024); FY2024 up 16.6% year over year (fact IDs 1345337, 1345349, 1345358).\n- Revenue (RevenueFromContractWithCustomerExcludingAssessedTax): $7,245M → $8,971M → $10,984M (IDs 1349396, 1349408, 1349417).\n- Operating expenses as a share of revenue (derived): 73.4% (FY2022) → 70.1% (FY2023) → 66.8% (FY2024) — a cumulative decline of about 6.6 percentage points over two years, i.e., meaningful operating leverage.\n\n**Mix by function (share of revenue, derived):**\n\n| Line | FY2022 | FY2023 | FY2024 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Sales & marketing | 38.8% | 36.8%* | 35.1% |\n| Research & development | 24.4% | 23.7%* | 23.2% |\n| General & administrative | 10.1% | 9.6%* | 8.5% |\n\n*FY2023 percentages computed from the same retrieved dollar values ($3,301M S&M, $2,124M R&D, $863M G&A; IDs 1349888, 1349120, 1341228) divided by FY2023 revenue; the FY2024 ratios were computed directly by tool.\n\nAbsolute dollars rose in every function (S&M $2,814M→$3,301M→$3,854M; R&D $1,768M→$2,124M→$2,543M; G&A $735M→$863M→$936M), so the improvement is a matter of scaling, not absolute cuts. The largest relative efficiency gain came in G&A (down ~1.6 pts of revenue) and sales & marketing (down ~3.7 pts), while R&D held roughly steady near 23–24%, consistent with continued investment.\n\n**Cost of revenue** also declined as a share of revenue: $1,573M (21.7% of FY2022 revenue) → $1,921M → $2,287M (20.8% of FY2024 revenue; IDs 1338234, 1338246, 1338255), reinforcing the margin trend.\n\n**Caveats:** These are derived ratios from reported GAAP line items, not company-disclosed margin targets; the database contains only the FY2024 annual report snapshot, so FY2022–FY2023 figures are the comparative amounts in that filing (they match earlier filings where duplicated). The final cost-of-revenue percentage for FY2024 was computed by tool; the FY2022 cost-of-revenue percentage (21.7%) is a simple division of the retrieved values and was not run through the calculator before the tool budget was exhausted."}, "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 10286, "completion_tokens": 774, "total_tokens": 11060, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 2304}, "prompt_cache_hit_tokens": 2304, "prompt_cache_miss_tokens": 7982}, "finish_reason": "stop", "attempts": 1}
